tern response was united and  consistent basically calling putin on  his bluff at that point putin did not  have much choice since he's been  posturing war for months a retweet would  be a major loss of faith obviously after  which russian military threats would not  be taken as seriously so russia had to  go ahead at this point essentially just  making [ __ ] up along the way accusing  ukraine of suddenly wanting to invade  the donbass in service of this some  hasty false flag attempts have followed  which were bordering on ridiculous  russians claimed ukrainians shot rockets  into russian territory then they said  ukrainians destroyed a russian border  checkpoint but of course anyone with an  iq above room temperature can see the  problems here according to russia here  once they pull their troops to the  border and threaten with defending the  local russian population that's when the  ukrainians suddenly decide to start  provoking them a country with the  world's most nuclear weapons and an army  five times the size right very cool then  russians aired footage of supposedly  ukrainian troops assaulting yet another  russian border checkpoint but  fortunately and conveniently for russian  media they apparently recorded the  entire thing on a gopro or something  right then separatists claimed  ukrainians blew up the core of one of  their leaders as it was standing in an  empty parking lot with nobody in it  right and then there was a claim that  ukrainians blew up a gas pipeline in the  lewis region also that they are shooting  at the civilian electrical  infrastructure showing a picture of a  single torn wire with some smoking  vegetation around it so once again  according to russian propaganda  ukrainians did not invade the dumbass  for 8 years of conflict but they wanted  to do so now when russia pulled 150 000  troops to the border threatening a  full-scale invasion under the pretext of  protecting russian speakers alright and  the reason why all these false flags  were so half-picked in my opinion is  because as i've said this is a hasty  plan b and a solid clue to this is  putin's hour-long disjointed borderline  unhinged rambling about ukraine  following the recognition of the  separate hysterias where he persists to  invoke ethno-nationalist justifications  between incoherent historical statements  the effect of russian invasion wasn't so  clear cut from the beginning there was  certainly some power play around the  russian government as there are  influential people within and without  who aren't necessarily in favor of  invasion for example the russian  military elite would not be too happy  with the concept of losing thousands of  russian soldiers in an invasion against  a supposedly fraternal country sanctions  are also a factor not just for the  economy as a whole but also for the  russian business elite and while russia  has built up massive financial reserves  over the years eventually sanctions will  start to bite not to mention the  presence of those reserves will hardly  be felt by ordinary russians social  issues can and will lead to instability  which pushing cannot afford so the way i  see it putin has basically trapped  himself in this situation if they stop  now all they'll have achieved is making  the separatist regions official which  they controlled anyway but those are  also economic black holes with destroyed  assets and infrastructure with most of  the population gone and for this they  get sanctioned and turned into  international pariahs not to mention  nord stream 2 which is now suspended  indefinitely and putin can't really  backpedal at this point this was his  rubicon and he crossed it aliyak daest  as they say at this point the only  potentially beneficial choice for putin  is to press on and try to achieve his  strategic goals within ukraine this  includes the land bridge to crimea  severing ukraine from the black sea and  as a worst-case scenario annexing the  entire country up to the carpathians but  these options also present their unique  problems for russia ukraine is currently  experiencing warmer wet weather meaning  the ground couldn't freeze enough to  allow quick passage for armored vehicles  and the north and east of the country  during the thaw are practically  quagmires this negates the possibility  of a blitzkrieg meaning the defenders  can better prepare and potentially do  more damage to the russian army  struggling in the mud also as a rule of  thumb attackers tend to lose more troops  and equipment than defenders western  provided weaponry is also a major  problem ukraine now has all sorts of  advanced hardware which can do serious  damage to russian hardware so even  though the russian army is larger and  more powerful the unfavorable terrain  the defender's edge plus western weapons  risk inflicting heavy casualties on  troops whose morale is not that high to  begin with this is not crimea it won't  be a short bloodless campaign followed  by celebrations it'll be a long bloody  conflict leaving thousands dead waged  against a fraternal people in service of  the russian elites interests russian  soldiers stationed in ukraine are  treated rather badly to begin with the  moscow time is describing it as  nightmare conditions and these russian  soldiers are facing motivated defenders  with high morale hell bent on protecting  their home from invasion this would also  be russia's first large army logistical  undertaking since 1945 against a modern  mechanized military which is also a  first if they [ __ ] up at any point or if  ukrainians manage to sabotage their  supply chains enough things can go  downhill for the russian army rather  fast so as you can see things aren't so  straightforward for putin as one would  think in fact a worst case scenario  would be them taking severe losses due  to unexpectedly high resistance supply  chain problems sabotage and so on thus  the high casualties leading to severe  domestic instability back home which  then cascades into more logistical  problems for the army and loss of morale  which increases losses even further  rinse and repeat until russia simply  collapses under the weight of the crisis  it created and then the fun stuff begins  such as ukrainians taking by crimea and  the dumbass and the like this is of  course a less likely scenario but it's  likely enough to cause concern for putin  especially now that his approval ratings  are lower to begin with so this is my  informed guess about the situation it  could be that i'm wrong but so far  things seem to be lining up for example  the luhansk militants declared today  that as far as they're concerned the  entire luhansk region belongs to them  and of course they called on the  ukrainian army to pull back so yeah in  the meantime don't forget to like and  subscribe and i'll be seeing you next  time

